## 3) Certbot helper script (host) — `infra/certbot_issue.sh`

यह script VPS पर चलाएँ ताकि Let's Encrypt cert issue कर सकें।

```bash
#!/bin/bash
set -e
DOMAIN=$1
if [ -z "$DOMAIN" ]; then
  echo "Usage: $0 your-domain.example"
  exit 1
fi

# stop docker nginx if it's using port 80
echo "Stopping nginx container (if running) to free port 80..."
docker rm -f shiksha_nginx || true

# request cert (standalone)
sudo certbot certonly --standalone -d $DOMAIN -d www.$DOMAIN --non-interactive --agree-tos -m your-email@example.com

# after success, certs are in /etc/letsencrypt/live/$DOMAIN/
# make sure docker-compose mounts /etc/letsencrypt

echo "Certificates obtained. Don't forget to restart docker compose: docker compose up -d"
```

> **Important:** certbot needs port 80 free. Temporary stop nginx container or use certbot's `--nginx` plugin if nginx is on host (not in docker). We are using standalone method above.

