## 5) `infra/deploy.sh` — one-shot deploy on VPS

```bash
#!/bin/bash
set -e
# Usage: ./deploy.sh your-domain.example
DOMAIN=$1
if [ -z "$DOMAIN" ]; then
  echo "Usage: $0 your-domain.example"
  exit 1
fi

# 1. build and start containers (nginx may error before certs exist - that's OK)
docker compose up -d --build

# 2. Issue certs using certbot (this will stop nginx container if it listens on 80)
./infra/certbot_issue.sh $DOMAIN

# 3. restart compose so nginx picks up certs
docker compose down
docker compose up -d --build

echo "Deployment complete. Visit https://$DOMAIN"
```

Give this file executable: `chmod +x infra/deploy.sh` and `chmod +x infra/certbot_issue.sh`.

